From: RTP-LLM build owners <rtp-llm@alibaba-inc.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] pypi: fail closed when a locked artifact is unavailable

The requirements locks in this repository are the supply-chain identity. The
rules_python 0.33.2 pip extension currently ignores an exact hash when its
index entry is marked yanked, then creates a plain whl_library without
urls/sha256. That repository invokes pip again and can select different bytes.

Keep an exact-hash yanked artifact usable, because the lock still identifies
its bytes, and fail during module evaluation when no locked artifact is found.
This removes the silent pip fallback without changing the normal direct
download path.

Upstream tracking: no upstream issue filed; this is repository policy for locked
wheels and should be removed when the dependency is replaced by an upstream
fail-closed implementation.

Regression coverage: dependency lock checks and Bazel analysis must continue
to pass for the six public hubs; a missing or yanked locked artifact must fail
with an analysis-time diagnostic instead of creating an unpinned repository.

Note: patch is generated without a/b prefixes, hence patch_strip = 0.
---
diff --git python/private/pypi/parse_requirements.bzl python/private/pypi/parse_requirements.bzl
index 8e0e5f6..8e0e5f6 100644
--- python/private/pypi/parse_requirements.bzl
+++ python/private/pypi/parse_requirements.bzl
@@ -451,17 +451,13 @@ def _add_dists(requirement, index_urls, python_version, logger = None):
     # TODO @aignas 2024-05-22: it is in theory possible to add all
     # requirements by version instead of by sha256. This may be useful
     # for some projects.
     for sha256 in requirement.srcs.shas:
-        # For now if the artifact is marked as yanked we just ignore it.
-        #
-        # See https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/simple-repository-api/#adding-yank-support-to-the-simple-api
-
         maybe_whl = index_urls.whls.get(sha256)
-        if maybe_whl and not maybe_whl.yanked:
+        if maybe_whl:
             whls.append(maybe_whl)
             continue
 
         maybe_sdist = index_urls.sdists.get(sha256)
-        if maybe_sdist and not maybe_sdist.yanked:
+        if maybe_sdist:
             sdist = maybe_sdist
             continue
 
diff --git python/private/pypi/extension.bzl python/private/pypi/extension.bzl
index 2f0e83e..2f0e83e 100644
--- python/private/pypi/extension.bzl
+++ python/private/pypi/extension.bzl
@@ -311,2 +311,8 @@ def _create_whl_repos(module_ctx, pip_attr, whl_map, whl_overrides, group_map, s
         elif get_index_urls:
-            logger.warn(lambda: "falling back to pip for installing the right file for {}".format(requirement.requirement_line))
+            fail((
+                "No indexed distribution matched the locked hashes for '{requirement}' " +
+                "(hashes: {hashes}); refusing the pip fallback."
+            ).format(
+                requirement = requirement.requirement_line,
+                hashes = ", ".join(requirement.srcs.shas),
+            ))
